 ### Enum notes
 
 - **`EmploymentArrangement` no longer exists** (dropped 2026-05-30, migration `20260530140000_employment_type_reference`). `InternalHiringRequest` / `InternalJobOpening` / `OfferLetterTemplate` `.employmentArrangement` are `String` columns holding an `EmploymentType.code`. The 5 built-ins (PERMANENT, CONTRACT, FREELANCER, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP) are `isSystem: true` — relabel/deactivate OK, delete blocked; codes are immutable after creation.
 - **`PermissionAction`** carries eight post-fork additions beyond the base VIEW/CREATE/EDIT/DELETE/EXPORT/APPROVE/ASSIGN: `CREATE_REQUEST` (raise a hiring request), `REVEAL_CREDENTIALS` (audited credential decrypt, recruitment-platforms), `SIGN_AS_OWNER` (offer owner-signature), `SUBMIT` (İŞKUR — fire a draft at the government portal), `MANAGE_KEYS` (AI-interviewer/call-center/sales-training/whatsapp provider keys; seeded to **no** role — super-admin-only via CASL bypass), `MANAGE_CAMPAIGNS` (call-center/whatsapp bulk-outbound campaigns; also seeded to no role), `WITHDRAW` and `UNAPPROVE` (marketing — the two revocations of 2026-09-16, §5.7: `admin` holds both, `marketing-manager` holds `WITHDRAW`, migration `20260925100000_marketing_withdraw_unapprove`). Adding a CASL-mapped action requires ALL of: the schema enum value, `ACTION_MAP` + `AppAction` in `casl-ability.factory.ts`, and (usually) seed-matrix rows — not just the DB enum.
 - **`PermissionScope`** is `ALL | ASSIGNED_TO_ME | IN_MY_DEPARTMENT`. (The fork-era `OWN_COMPANY` / `ASSIGNED_ONLY` values were removed; any doc citing them is stale.)
 - **`InternalApplicantStage`'s legacy training-track debt is PAID (2026-09-14).** The five values (`SELECTED_FOR_TRAINING`, `IN_TRAINING`, `TRAINING_COMPLETE`, `DEPLOYMENT_READY`, `ACTIVE`) were dropped with the applicant Training LMS in migration `20260921103000_remove_legacy_training` — prod held 0 applicants on any of them, and removing the module removed the only way to reach them. The enum is now exactly the 10-stage hire ladder plus `REJECTED` / `ON_HOLD`; the migration recreated the type (Postgres cannot drop an enum value in place), recast the ONE dependent column (`internal_applicants.stage`, dropping and restoring its `'APPLIED'` default around the cast), and adopted schema.prisma's order — which moves `HIRED` to last, making the applicant list's cosmetic `sortBy=stage` more correct, not less. `NotificationType` still carries CRM-era values; that half of the §12.3 item remains open. There is **no `WITHDRAWN` stage** — withdrawal is `REJECTED` + `rejectionReason: WITHDREW`, mapped at the display layer only.
+- **`WEBSITE_*` values** (2026-09-19, migration `20260925120000_website_intake_door`): `NotificationType.WEBSITE_FORM_RECEIVED` / `WEBSITE_FORMS_UNAVAILABLE` and `ActivityType.WEBSITE_SUBMISSION_RECEIVED` / `_HANDLED` / `_FAILED` were added via `ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS` in the migration commit that ships alone, one deploy before any code reads them; the four `Website*` enums (`WebsiteFormKind`, `WebsiteSubmissionStatus`, `WebsiteSubscriberStatus`, `WebsiteTokenClass`) are mirrored in `packages/constants/src/enums/website.enums.ts` next to `WEBSITE_FORM_KEYS` / `WEBSITE_FORM_KIND_BY_KEY`, the one source of the ten form keys.
 
 ### Schema conventions
 
 - Singular `PascalCase` models, `camelCase` fields, `SCREAMING_SNAKE` enum values.
 - `createdAt` / `updatedAt` on every model; soft-delete via `deletedAt` where appropriate (leads, bank questions, market-research records…). The permanent applicant delete (2026-07-31) is the ONE sanctioned hard-delete in IR.
 - Enums live in the schema and are mirrored in `packages/constants` when the frontend imports them.
 - The country dimension is the **code** everywhere (`PK`, `TR`), cities are **names** — across IR, Market Research, Sales, Projects, İŞKUR gating.
 - Money is grouped **by currency** in every cross-record aggregate (projects reports, campaign ROI) — never summed across currencies.
 - Snapshot-style plain-string user references (no FK) are used where history must survive user deletion (`InternalInterviewParticipant.userId`, `MarketResearchVersion.snapshotById`, `WhatsappNotification.applicantId`). Any new FK-less `applicantId` column must be handled explicitly by the applicant hard-delete — grep before assuming the cascade is complete.
 
